        [
            'name' => 'To be a wonderer is no small feat - a few words about Polish Rovering',
            'description' => "Step into the path of the wonderer \u{2014} a young person who seeks meaning, challenge, and service. This workshop is inspired by the Polish Wonderer Code and the motto “Go into the world, see, think – help, that is, act.”\n\nTogether we’ll explore what it truly means to live as a wonderer: to look beyond what’s familiar, to discover your own path, and to open your eyes and heart to the world around you. Through reflection, discussion, and shared adventure, we’ll learn how wonderers combine curiosity with responsibility \u{2014} transforming exploration into action.\n\nJoin us if you’re ready to pause, think, and then move forward with purpose. The art of being a wonderer begins with a single step \u{2014} take yours with us!\n\nPřednáší: Oskar Pardyak + Maciej Ładoś\nSkautské téma\n\nWe are instructors of the Polish Scouting and Guiding Association (ZHP) and primarily work with the wonderer age section, serving as deputies to the Head of the Wonderer Department. This year, both of us organized our national wonderer event, which gathered nearly 1,000 participants. Maciek continues to be involved in this event, while Oskar focuses on topics related to civic education among wonderers.",
